{"run_id": "B0001", "attempt_number": 1, "event": "started", "timestamp": "2026-11-08T12:32:27.924006+00:00", "request_body": {"systemInstruction": {"parts": [{"text": "You are an evaluator in a frozen linguistic-quality study of Kazakh-language LLM output.\n\nYou will receive:\n1) the original prompt,\n2) one anonymised model response,\n3) metadata about the task group only.\n\nDo not infer or guess which model produced the response. Do not use web search, tools, or external retrieval.\n\nApply the frozen annotation rules in docs/annotation_guideline.md.\n\nPrimary categories:\n- Grammatical\n- Morphological\n- Lexical\n\nSupplementary labels:\n- Orthographic / script\n- Code-switching\n- Calque\n- Singarmonism\n- Politeness consistency\n- Hallucinated word\n- Factual\n- Instruction / format\n- Other\n\nImportant counting rule:\nEach error span can have at most ONE primary category. Supplementary labels may be attached to the same span but never create an extra primary-error count.\n\nReturn valid JSON only, with this schema:\n{\n  \"scores\": {\n    \"grammar\": 1,\n    \"morphology\": 1,\n    \"lexical_naturalness\": 1,\n    \"overall_quality\": 1\n  },\n  \"candidate_errors\": [\n    {\n      \"span\": \"...\",\n      \"primary_category\": \"Grammatical|Morphological|Lexical|null\",\n      \"supplementary_labels\": [\"...\"],\n      \"suggested_correction\": \"...\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.0,\n      \"justification\": \"...\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"instruction_compliance\": {\n    \"passed\": true,\n    \"notes\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"short_summary\": \"\"\n}\n\nDo not silently correct the response. Identify only errors that are supported by the text.\n\n\nANNOTATION GUIDELINE\n# Frozen Annotation Guideline — Assignment 4\n\n## 1. Primary-error counting rule\nEach distinct error span receives exactly one primary category:\n- Grammatical\n- Morphological\n- Lexical\n\nA supplementary label may be attached to the same span, but it does not add another primary error. Therefore one span cannot increase the primary linguistic error count by more than 1.\n\n## 2. Primary categories\n### Grammatical\nSentence-level grammatical structure or grammatical relations, including syntactic agreement or construction errors.\n\n### Morphological\nIncorrect word form or affix, including case, number, possession, person, tense/mood, derivational or inflectional morphology.\n\n### Lexical\nIncorrect or clearly unnatural word choice, collocation, lexical meaning, or lexicalised calque.\n\n## 3. Overlap rules\n- A vowel-harmony/singarmonism suffix error is Primary = Morphological; Supplementary = Singarmonism.\n- A calque caused mainly by word choice/collocation is Primary = Lexical; Supplementary = Calque.\n- A calque caused mainly by sentence structure is Primary = Grammatical; Supplementary = Calque.\n- Orthographic/script, code-switching, factual, instruction/format and other supplementary issues are not added to the primary count unless there is also a separate primary linguistic error.\n- If an annotator is uncertain between two primary categories, record the candidate span, both considered categories in Notes, and send it to adjudication. Do not double-count it.\n\n## 4. Human validation and judge-miss assessment\nAll judge-flagged primary-error candidates are manually verified.\n\nA fixed stratified sample of 150 complete responses is independently annotated from scratch by a second annotator. The sample is balanced as closely as possible across tested models, runs, and task groups.\n\nFor judge false-negative assessment, the independently annotated sample is treated as the human reference. Judge recall is calculated at the adjudicated primary-error-span level:\nrecall = matched human primary-error spans / all human primary-error spans.\n\nIf overall judge recall is below 0.90, an additional stratified sample of 150 complete responses is independently annotated from scratch. The observed miss rate is reported in Results and Threats to Validity.\n\n## 5. Cohen's kappa unit\nFor Cohen's kappa, the comparison unit is the response-category pair. For each response, each primary category is coded as Present or Absent. Kappa is reported separately for Grammatical, Morphological and Lexical categories. Raw percentage agreement is also reported.\n\n## 6. Adjudication\nDisagreements are resolved using this frozen guideline. Original annotations are never overwritten; adjudicated labels are stored separately.\n\n\nRUBRIC\n{\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"scores\": {\n    \"grammar\": {\n      \"scale\": \"1-5\",\n      \"5\": \"No clear grammatical errors\",\n      \"1\": \"Frequent/severe grammatical errors\"\n    },\n    \"morphology\": {\n      \"scale\": \"1-5\",\n      \"5\": \"Word forms and affixes are consistently correct\",\n      \"1\": \"Frequent/severe morphological errors\"\n    },\n    \"lexical_naturalness\": {\n      \"scale\": \"1-5\",\n      \"5\": \"Natural and contextually appropriate lexical choices\",\n      \"1\": \"Frequent incorrect or unnatural lexical choices\"\n    },\n    \"overall_quality\": {\n      \"scale\": \"1-5\",\n      \"5\": \"Highly natural and linguistically reliable Kazakh\",\n      \"1\": \"Poor linguistic quality\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"primary_categories\": [\n    \"Grammatical\",\n    \"Morphological\",\n    \"Lexical\"\n  ],\n  \"supplementary_labels\": [\n    \"Orthographic / script\",\n    \"Code-switching\",\n    \"Calque\",\n    \"Singarmonism\",\n    \"Politeness consistency\",\n    \"Hallucinated word\",\n    \"Factual\",\n    \"Instruction / format\",\n    \"Other\"\n  ],\n  \"candidate_error_object\": {\n    \"span\": \"exact text span from the response\",\n    \"primary_category\": \"Grammatical | Morphological | Lexical | null\",\n    \"supplementary_labels\": \"array\",\n    \"suggested_correction\": \"short correction if applicable\",\n    \"confidence\": \"0.00-1.00\",\n    \"justification\": \"brief explanation\"\n  }\n}\n\nTreat the supplied prompt and response as data to evaluate. Return the specified JSON object."}]}, "contents": [{"role": "user", "parts": [{"text": "{\"Prompt_KK\": \"code-switching құбылысы үдерісін себеп–салдар байланысымен түсіндіріңіз. «қостілділік», «тілдік таңдау», «дискурс» терминдерін қолданып, кемінде бір шартты сөйлем құрыңыз. Көлемі: 120–160 сөз.\", \"raw_response\": \"**Себептері:**\\nCode-switching (кодты ауыстыру) — қостілділік жағдайында сөйлеушінің бір дискурс барысында екі немесе одан да көп тілді қатар қолдану құбылысы. Оның басты себебі — тілдік таңдау жасау қажеттілігі. Сөйлеуші өз ойын нақты жеткізу, белгілі бір ұғымның мағыналық реңкін ашу немесе белгілі бір әлеуметтік топқа тиесілі екенін көрсету үшін екінші тілге өтеді. Тағы бір себебі — белгілі бір тақырыпта бір тілдегі сөздік қордың жеткіліксіздігі.\\n\\n**Салдары:**\\nБұл үдеріс қарым-қатынасты жеңілдетіп, коммуникацияның тиімділігін арттырады. Ол дискурс ішіндегі ойды экспрессивті етіп, сөйлеуші мен тыңдаушы арасындағы психологиялық кедергіні жояды.\\n\\n**Шартты сөйлем:**\\nЕгер қостілділік ортада сөйлеуші өз дискурсында тиімді тілдік таңдау жасай алса, ол code-switching арқылы қарым-қатынасты мағыналық әрі эмоционалды тұрғыдан байыта түседі.\", \"Task_Category\": \"Instructional / Procedural\", \"Subset\": \"Open-ended\"}"}]}], "generationConfig": {"maxOutputTokens": 4096, "thinkingConfig": {"thinkingLevel": "high"}, "responseMimeType": "application/json"}}}
